    markdown:
      "## complete\n\n`client.fleetify.routes.steps.complete(routeID: string, stepID: string, key: string, document?: object, mode?: string, status?: string): void`\n\n**patch** `/fleetify/routes/{routeID}/steps/{stepID}`\n\nComplete a route step with document submission, or update the document of a completed route step.\n\nWhen all steps are completed, the encapsulating route’s status will change to completed automatically.\n\nEither Session Token must be provided to authenticate the request.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `routeID: string`\n\n- `stepID: string`\n\n- `key: string`\n  A key is a unique identifier that is required to authenticate a request to the API.\n\n- `document?: object`\n  A key-value map storing form submission data, where keys correspond to field labels and values can be of any type depend on the type of according document item.\n\n- `mode?: string`\n  Sets the status of the route step. Currently only completed is supported.\n\nNote: once marked completed, a step cannot transition to other statuses. You can only update the document afterwards.\n\n- `status?: string`\n  Sets the status of the route step. Currently only completed is supported.\n\nNote: once marked completed, a step cannot transition to other statuses. You can only update the document afterwards.\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport NextbillionSDK from '@nbai/sdk';\n\nconst client = new NextbillionSDK();\n\nawait client.fleetify.routes.steps.complete('stepID', { routeID: 'routeID', key: 'key' })\n```",
