    response: '{ id?: string; error?: string; status?: string; timestamp?: number; }',
    markdown:
      "## subscribe\n\n`client.skynet.subscribe(action: 'TRIP_SUBSCRIBE' | 'TRIP_UNSUBSCRIBE' | 'HEARTBEAT', id?: string, params?: { id: string; }): { id?: string; error?: string; status?: string; timestamp?: number; }`\n\n**post** `/skynet/subscribe`\n\nPOST Action\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `action: 'TRIP_SUBSCRIBE' | 'TRIP_UNSUBSCRIBE' | 'HEARTBEAT'`\n  Specify the behavior that needs to be achieved for the subscription. Following values are accepted:\n\n*   TRIP\\_SUBSCRIBE: Enable a trip subscription.\n    \n*   TRIP\\_UNSUBSCRIBE: Unsubscribe from a trip\n    \n*   HEARTBEAT: Enable heartbeat mechanism for a web-socket connection. The action message need to be sent at a frequency higher than every 5 mins to keep the connection alive. Alternatively, users can chose to respond to the ping frame sent by web socket server to keep the connection alive. Refer to [connection details](https://188--nbai-docs-stg.netlify.app/docs/tracking/api/live-tracking-api#connect-to-web-socket-server) for more details.\n\n- `id?: string`\n  Specify a custom ID for the subscription. It can be used to reference a given subscription in the downstream applications / systems.\n\n- `params?: { id: string; }`\n  - `id: string`\n    Specify the ID of an active trip that needs to be subscribed. The ID of a trip is returned in the response when _Start A Trip_ request is acknowledged.\n\nThis attribute is mandatory when action is set to either \"TRIP\\_SUBSCRIBE\" or \"TRIP\\_UNSUBSCRIBE\"\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ id?: string; error?: string; status?: string; timestamp?: number; }`\n\n  - `id?: string`\n  - `error?: string`\n  - `status?: string`\n  - `timestamp?: number`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport NextbillionSDK from '@nbai/sdk';\n\nconst client = new NextbillionSDK();\n\nconst response = await client.skynet.subscribe({ action: 'TRIP_SUBSCRIBE' });\n\nconsole.log(response);\n```",
