      "## retrieve\n\n`client.skynet.monitor.retrieve(id: string, key: string): { data?: object; message?: string; status?: string; }`\n\n**get** `/skynet/monitor/{id}`\n\nGet a Monitor\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `id: string`\n\n- `key: string`\n  A key is a unique identifier that is required to authenticate a request to the API.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ data?: { monitor?: object; }; message?: string; status?: string; }`\n\n  - `data?: { monitor?: { id?: string; created_at?: number; description?: string; geofence_config?: { geofence_ids?: string[]; }; geofences?: string[]; idle_config?: { distance_tolerance?: number; time_tolerance?: number; }; match_filter?: { include_all_of_attributes?: object; include_any_of_attributes?: object; }; meta_data?: object; name?: string; speeding_config?: { customer_speed_limit?: number; time_tolerance?: number; use_admin_speed_limit?: boolean; }; tags?: string[]; type?: 'enter' | 'exit' | 'enter_and_exit' | 'speeding' | 'idle'; updated_at?: number; }; }`\n  - `message?: string`\n  - `status?: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport NextbillionSDK from '@nbai/sdk';\n\nconst client = new NextbillionSDK();\n\nconst monitor = await client.skynet.monitor.retrieve('id', { key: 'key=API_KEY' });\n\nconsole.log(monitor);\n```",
