    markdown:
      "## retrieve\n\n`client.skynet.trip.retrieve(id: string, key: string, cluster?: 'america'): { data?: object; message?: string; status?: string; }`\n\n**get** `/skynet/trip/{id}`\n\nRetrieves detailed information about a specific trip.\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `id: string`\n\n- `key: string`\n  A key is a unique identifier that is required to authenticate a request to the API.\n\n- `cluster?: 'america'`\n  the cluster of the region you want to use\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ data?: { trip?: { id?: string; asset_id?: string; attributes?: object; created_at?: number; description?: string; ended_at?: number; meta_data?: object; name?: string; route?: track_location[]; started_at?: number; state?: string; stops?: trip_stop[]; updated_at?: number; }; }; message?: string; status?: string; }`\n\n  - `data?: { trip?: { id?: string; asset_id?: string; attributes?: object; created_at?: number; description?: string; ended_at?: number; meta_data?: object; name?: string; route?: { accuracy?: number; altitude?: number; battery_level?: number; bearing?: number; location?: object; meta_data?: object; speed?: number; timestamp?: number; tracking_mode?: string; }[]; started_at?: number; state?: string; stops?: { geofence_id?: string; meta_data?: object; name?: string; }[]; updated_at?: number; }; }`\n  - `message?: string`\n  - `status?: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport NextbillionSDK from '@nbai/sdk';\n\nconst client = new NextbillionSDK();\n\nconst trip = await client.skynet.trip.retrieve('id', { key: 'key=API_KEY' });\n\nconsole.log(trip);\n```",
