    markdown:
      "## list\n\n`client.geofence.list(key: string, pn?: number, ps?: number, tags?: string): { data?: object; status?: string; }`\n\n**get** `/geofence/list`\n\nGet Geofence List\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `key: string`\n  A key is a unique identifier that is required to authenticate a request to the API.\n\n- `pn?: number`\n  Denotes page number. Use this along with the ps parameter to implement pagination for your searched results. This parameter does not have a maximum limit but would return an empty response in case a higher value is provided when the result-set itself is smaller.\n\n- `ps?: number`\n  Denotes number of search results per page. Use this along with the pn parameter to implement pagination for your searched results.\n\n- `tags?: string`\n  Comma (,) separated list of tags which will be used to filter the geofences.\n\nPlease note only the geofences which have all the tags added to this parameter will be included in the result. This parameter can accept a string with a maximum length of 256 characters.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ data?: { list?: object[]; page?: object; }; status?: string; }`\n\n  - `data?: { list?: { id?: string; circle_center?: { lat?: number; lon?: number; }; circle_radius?: number; created_at?: number; geojson?: object; ic_contours_meter?: number; ic_contours_minute?: number; ic_coordinates?: string; ic_denoise?: number; ic_departure_time?: number; ic_mode?: number; meta_data?: object; name?: string; tags?: string[]; type?: 'circle' | 'polygon' | 'isochrone'; updated_at?: number; }[]; page?: { hasmore?: boolean; page?: number; size?: number; total?: number; }; }`\n  - `status?: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport NextbillionSDK from '@nbai/sdk';\n\nconst client = new NextbillionSDK();\n\nconst geofences = await client.geofence.list({ key: 'key=API_KEY' });\n\nconsole.log(geofences);\n```",
