      "## contains\n\n`client.geofence.contains(key: string, locations: string, geofences?: string, verbose?: string): { data?: object; status?: string; }`\n\n**get** `/geofence/contain`\n\nGeofence Contains\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `key: string`\n  A key is a unique identifier that is required to authenticate a request to the API.\n\n- `locations: string`\n  Pipe (|) separated coordinates, in [latitude,longitude] format, of the locations to be searched against the geofences.\n\n- `geofences?: string`\n  A , separated list geofence IDs against which the locations will be searched. If not provided, then the 'locations' will be searched against all your existing geofences.\n\nMaximum length of the string can be 256 characters.\n\n- `verbose?: string`\n  When true, an array with detailed information of geofences is returned. When false, an array containing only the IDs of the geofences is returned.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ data?: { result_list?: { geofence_detail?: geofence; geofence_id?: string; result?: object[]; }[]; }; status?: string; }`\n\n  - `data?: { result_list?: { geofence_detail?: { id?: string; circle_center?: object; circle_radius?: number; created_at?: number; geojson?: polygon_geojson; ic_contours_meter?: number; ic_contours_minute?: number; ic_coordinates?: string; ic_denoise?: number; ic_departure_time?: number; ic_mode?: number; meta_data?: object; name?: string; tags?: string[]; type?: 'circle' | 'polygon' | 'isochrone'; updated_at?: number; }; geofence_id?: string; result?: { contain?: boolean; location_index?: number; }[]; }[]; }`\n  - `status?: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport NextbillionSDK from '@nbai/sdk';\n\nconst client = new NextbillionSDK();\n\nconst response = await client.geofence.contains({ key: 'key=API_KEY', locations: '13.25805884388484,77.91083661048299|13.25805884388484,77.91083661048299' });\n\nconsole.log(response);\n```",
