    name: 'get_distance_matrix_status',
    endpoint: '/mdm/status',
    httpMethod: 'get',
    summary: 'Get Asynchronous Distance Matrix Status',
    description: 'Get massive distance matrix task status',
    stainlessPath: '(resource) mdm > (method) get_distance_matrix_status',
    qualified: 'client.mdm.getDistanceMatrixStatus',
    params: ['id: string;', 'key: string;'],
    response:
      "{ code?: 'Ok' | 'Processing' | 'Failed'; output_addr?: string; result_link?: string; status?: string; }",
    markdown:
      "## get_distance_matrix_status\n\n`client.mdm.getDistanceMatrixStatus(id: string, key: string): { code?: 'Ok' | 'Processing' | 'Failed'; output_addr?: string; result_link?: string; status?: string; }`\n\n**get** `/mdm/status`\n\nGet massive distance matrix task status\n\n### Parameters\n\n- `id: string`\n  Provide the unique ID that was returned on successful submission of the Asynchronous Distance Matrix POST request.\n\n- `key: string`\n  A key is a unique identifier that is required to authenticate a request to the API.\n\n### Returns\n\n- `{ code?: 'Ok' | 'Processing' | 'Failed'; output_addr?: string; result_link?: string; status?: string; }`\n\n  - `code?: 'Ok' | 'Processing' | 'Failed'`\n  - `output_addr?: string`\n  - `result_link?: string`\n  - `status?: string`\n\n### Example\n\n```typescript\nimport NextbillionSDK from '@nbai/sdk';\n\nconst client = new NextbillionSDK();\n\nconst response = await client.mdm.getDistanceMatrixStatus({ id: 'id', key: 'key=API_KEY' });\n\nconsole.log(response);\n```",
